# The image ships the whole repo on purpose — `agent/instructions.md`, `roles/<role>.md` and
# `agent/skills/*/SKILL.md` are read off disk at `process.cwd()`, not imported, so a standalone
# bundle would boot and then throw on the first turn. This list is what must NOT come along.

# Rebuilt inside the image, and platform-specific: the Agent SDK's native binary is an
# optionalDependency resolved per OS and libc, so a macOS node_modules would be the wrong one.
node_modules
.next
*.tsbuildinfo
dist
.output
.nitro

# Credentials. The container reads its env from `env_file` at run time; a token baked into a layer
# is a token in the registry.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.vercel
.DS_Store

# The stale second lockfile — pnpm is the package manager here.
package-lock.json
